        "id": "sec-01",
        "answerable": true,
        "answered": true,
        "refused_by_strict_check": false,
        "decision_correct": true,
        "answer": "To require an OAuth2 bearer token on an endpoint, you can use the `OAuth2PasswordBearer` class from FastAPI's security module, and pass the `tokenUrl` parameter to it [1]. This parameter specifies the URL that the client (the frontend running in the user's browser) will use to send the `username` and `password` in order to get a token [1].\n\nFor example:\n```python\nfrom fastapi import Depends\nfrom fastapi.security import OAuth2PasswordBearer\nfrom fastapi import HTTPException\n\noauth2_scheme = OAuth2PasswordBearer(tokenUrl=\"token\")\n\n@app.get(\"/items/\")\nasync def read_items(token: str = Depends(oauth2_scheme)):\n    return {\"token\": token}\n```\nThis code defines an endpoint `/items/` that requires an OAuth2 bearer token to be passed in the `Authorization` header [2]. The `Depends` function is used to specify that the `token` parameter should be validated using the `oauth2_scheme` instance [2].\n\nYou can also use the `Annotated` version if possible, as it provides more type safety [3]. For example:\n```python\nfrom fastapi import Depends\nfrom fastapi.security import OAuth2PasswordBearer\nfrom fastapi import HTTPException\nfrom typing import Annotated\n\noauth2_scheme = OAuth2PasswordBearer(tokenUrl=\"token\")\n\n@app.get(\"/items/\")\nasync def read_items(token: Annotated[str, Depends(oauth2_scheme)]):\n    return {\"token\": token}\n```\nThis code defines an endpoint `/items/` that requires an OAuth2 bearer token to be passed in the `Authorization` header [4]. The `Depends` function is used to specify that the `token` parameter should be validated using the `oauth2_scheme` instance [4].\n\nNote that the `tokenUrl` parameter specifies the URL that the client will use to send the `username` and `password` in order to get a token [5]. This URL is used to send the request to the API to obtain the token.\n\nAlso, the `Depends` function is used to specify that the `token` parameter should be validated using the `oauth2_scheme` instance [3]. This allows FastAPI to integrate the security scheme with OpenAPI and provide automatic API documentation.\n\nIn summary, to require an OAuth2 bearer token on an endpoint, you can use the `OAuth2PasswordBearer` class from FastAPI's security module, and pass the `tokenUrl` parameter to it. This parameter specifies the URL that the client will use to send the `username` and `password` in order to get a token. The `Depends` function is used to specify that the `token` parameter should be validated using the `oauth2_scheme` instance.",
